; the empty sum: `sum i (a, b) T` is 0 for every range with a > b (todo 78; before, only for a = b + 1), and
; "sum-last" needs a <= b + 1 -- without that premise the two rules proved `3 = 0`
load analysis
calc on

; every range with a > b is empty
5 > 3
(sum i (5, 3) i) = 0
5 > 2
(sum i (5, 2) i) = 0
1 > 0
(sum i (1, 0) (i * i)) = 0

; a range of one term, and one more term
(sum i (2, 2) i) = 2
1 <= 2 + 1
(sum i (1, 2 + 1) i) = (2 + 1) + (sum i (1, 2) i)

; "sum-last" does not apply to a range that is empty by more than one: this was the derivation of `3 = 0`
expect "ProofError"
    (sum i (5, 2 + 1) i) = (2 + 1) + (sum i (5, 2) i)
